DESCRIPTION >
    Wave-3 flexible_report Class-A dim-swap: group_by=PROVIDER. Clone of flexible_report_main_by_site
    with the dim expr swapped to GROUP_COLUMNS.provider (PROVIDER_SQL, attribution-engine.js:79) and
    the SAME external_event_id dedup carried from birth (#170). One row per provider with the metric.

    MODEL-INDEPENDENT: provider is a CONVERSION-PROPERTY group_by — GROUP_COLUMNS.provider = PROVIDER_SQL
    for all 4 touch models (first_touch/last_touch/first_touch_non_direct/last_touch_non_direct), and it
    references NO _nd touchpoint columns. For the *_non_direct models the live sql adds a _nd LEFT JOIN
    that the provider dim never reads; that join is 1:<=1 by distinct_id (non-fanning), so count()/SUM
    per provider is identical whether or not it runs. Omitting it here is value-identical -> this ONE
    pipe serves group_by=provider for all 4 touch models. (last_touch_non_direct+provider is the live
    prod 504 this pipe fixes.)

    dim = PROVIDER_SQL, typed-translated (§2.6): properties.provider -> provider (LowCardinality(
    Nullable(String)), events.datasource:33); properties.ingestion_method -> ingestion_method
    (LowCardinality(String), :32). metric in {revenue, conversions} via the `metric` param.
    BASE-CASE GATE ONLY (no dim2/custom/window/filters, UTC, conversion_date) — everything else falls
    to HogQL. Same params/output columns (dim_value, metric_value) as the base pipe so the wiring's
    positional remap stays byte-identical.

    external_event_id DEDUP (identical to flexible_report_main_by_site, #170): keep all null/empty-keyed
    rows; for a non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered,
    matching HogQL). Tie-break event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — parity holds because a genuine duplicate
    shares provider+value. PARAM SHAPE: {{ String(site_id) }} referenced TWICE (outer + dedup subquery);
    date params once. MANDATORY before deploy: `tb --cloud deploy --check`. VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN.

NODE flexible_report_provider_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(NULLIF(provider, ''), multiIf(ingestion_method = 'server_routed', 'browser', ingestion_method = 'offline', 'payments_api', 'unknown')) AS dim_value,
        {% if String(metric, 'conversions') == 'revenue' %}
        SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)))
        {% else %}
        count()
        {% end %} AS metric_value
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
      -- external_event_id dedup — carried from flexible_report_main_by_site (#170), faithful port of
      -- the HogQL leg (attribution-engine.js:2397-2409). KEEP every null/empty-keyed row; for a
      -- non-null key keep the GLOBAL-earliest-by-timestamp row (inner subquery NOT date-filtered).
      -- Tie-break Tinybird event_id (HogQL uses uuid) — identical bucket for a genuine duplicate.
      AND (
        external_event_id IS NULL
        OR external_event_id = ''
        OR event_id IN (
          SELECT argMin(event_id, timestamp)
          FROM events
          WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
            AND event_type = '$conversion'
            AND external_event_id IS NOT NULL
            AND external_event_id != ''
          GROUP BY external_event_id
        )
      )
    GROUP BY dim_value
    ORDER BY metric_value DESC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
